{
  "book.name": {
    "value": "The Hexbook",
    "comment": "The book's title; every book.* text is a page of thehexbook (ported from Hex Casting)"
  },
  "book.category.basics": "Getting Started",
  "book.category.basics.desc": "The practitioners of this art would cast their so-called Hexes by drawing strange patterns in the air with a Staff -- or craft powerful magical items to do the casting for them. How might I do the same?",
  "book.category.patterns": "Patterns",
  "book.category.patterns.desc": "A list of all the patterns I've discovered, as well as what they do.",
  "book.entry.media": "Media",
  "book.entry.media.page1": "Media is a form of mental energy external to a mind. All living creatures generate trace amounts of media when thinking about anything; after the thought is finished, the media is released into the environment.",
  "book.entry.media.page2": "The art of casting Hexes is all about manipulating media to do your bidding.\nMedia can exert influences on other media-- the strength and type of influence can be manipulated by drawing media out into patterns.",
  "book.entry.media.page3": "Scholars of the art used a concentrated blob of media on the end of a stick: by waving it in the air in precise configurations, they were able to manipulate enough media with enough precision to influence the world itself, in the form of a Hex.",
  "book.entry.media.page4": "Sadly, even a fully sentient being (like myself, presumably) can only generate miniscule amounts of media. It would be quite impractical to try and use my own brainpower to cast Hexes.",
  "book.entry.media.page5": "But legend has it that there are underground deposits where media slowly accumulates, growing into crystalline forms.\nIf I could just find one of those...",
  "book.entry.geodes": "Geodes",
  "book.entry.geodes.page1": "Aha! While mining deep underground, I found an enormous geode resonating with energy-- energy which pressed against my skull and my thoughts. And now, I hold that pressure in my hand, in solid form. That proves it.",
  "book.entry.geodes.page2": "This must be the place spoken about in legends where media accumulates.",
  "book.entry.geodes.page3": "These amethyst crystals must be a convenient, solidified form of Media.",
  "book.entry.geodes.page4": "It appears that, in addition to the Amethyst Shards I have seen in the past, these crystals can also drop bits of powdered Amethyst Dust, as well as these Charged Amethyst Crystals.",
  "book.entry.geodes.page5": "It looks like I'll have a better chance of finding the Charged Amethyst Crystals by using a Fortune pickaxe.",
  "book.entry.geodes.page6": "As I take the beauty of the crystal in, I can feel connections flashing wildly in my mind. It's like the media in the air is entering me, empowering me, elucidating me... It feels wonderful.",
  "book.entry.geodes.page7": "Finally, my study into the arcane is starting to make some sense!\nLet me reread those old legends again, now that I know what I'm looking at.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast": "A Frustration",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page1": "Argh! Why won't it let me cast the spell?!\nThe scroll I found rings with authenticity. I can feel it humming in the scroll-- the pattern is true, or as true as it can be. The spell is right there.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page2": "But it feels as if it's on the other side of some thin membrane. I called it-- it tried to manifest-- yet it COULD NOT.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page3": "It felt like the barrier may have weakened ever so slightly from the force that I exerted on the spell; yet despite my greatest efforts-- my deepest focus, my finest amethyst, my precisest drawings-- it refuses to cross the barrier.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page4": "It's maddening.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page5": "This is where my arcane studies end? Cursed by impotence, cursed to lose my rightful powers?\nI should take a deep breath. I should meditate on what I have learned, even if it wasn't very much...",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page6": "...After careful reflection... I have discovered a change in myself.\nIt seems... in lieu of amethyst, I've unlocked the ability to cast spells using my own mind and life energy-- just as I read of in the legends of old.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page7": "I'm not sure why I can now. It's just... the truth-knowledge-burden was always there, and I see it now. I know it. I bear it.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page8": "Fortunately, I feel my limits as well-- I would get approximately two Charged Amethyst's worth of media out of my health at its prime.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page9": "I shudder to even consider it-- I've kept my mind mostly intact so far, in my studies. But the fact is-- I form one side of a tenuous link.",
  "book.entry.couldnt_cast.page10": "I'm connected to some other side-- a side whose boundary has thinned from that trauma. A place where simple actions spell out eternal glory.\nIs it so wrong, to want it for myself?",
  "book.entry.start_to_see": "WHAT DID I SEE",
  "book.entry.start_to_see.page1": "The texts weren't lying. Nature took its due.\nThat... that was...",
  "book.entry.start_to_see.page2": "...that was one of the worst things I've ever experienced. I offered my plan to Nature, and got a firm smile and a tearing sensation in return-- a piece of myself breaking away, like amethyst dust in the rain.",
  "book.entry.start_to_see.page3": "I feel lucky to have survived, much less have the sagacity to write this-- I should declare the matter closed, double-check my math before I cast any more Hexes, and never make such a mistake again.\n...But.",
  "book.entry.start_to_see.page4": "But for the scarcest instant, that part of myself... it saw... something. A place-- a design, perhaps? (Such distinctions didn't seem to matter in the face of... that.)",
  "book.entry.start_to_see.page5": "And a... a membrane-barrier-skin-border, separating myself from a realm of raw thought-flow-light-energy. I remember-- I saw-thought-recalled-felt-- the barrier fuzzing at its edges, just so slightly.\nI wanted through.",
  "book.entry.start_to_see.page6": "I shouldn't. I know I shouldn't. It's dangerous. It's too dangerous. The force required... I'd have to bring myself within a hair's breadth of Death itself with a single stroke.\nBut I'm. So. Close.",
  "book.entry.start_to_see.page7": "This is the culmination of my art. This is the Enlightenment I've been seeking.\nI want more. I need to see it again. I will see it.\nWhat is my mortal mind against immortal glory?",
  "book.entry.patterns_intro": "Patterns Introduction",
  "book.entry.patterns_intro.page1": "Patterns are the building blocks of every Hex. Each one is a sequence of straight lines drawn across the dots of the casting grid.",
  "book.entry.patterns_intro.page2": "Draw a pattern by dragging across the grid; release to cast it. Sneak and use the staff to clear your stack."
}